1
00:00:04,045 --> 00:00:06,047
[PANTING]

2
00:00:08,341 --> 00:00:11,302
Having a little trouble
catching your breath, there?

3
00:00:12,094 --> 00:00:16,594
No, I'm good. If my P.E. teachers had
told me this is what I was training for...

4
00:00:16,849 --> 00:00:18,225
I would have tried a lot harder.

5
00:00:18,392 --> 00:00:20,394
[LAUGHS]

6
00:00:21,145 --> 00:00:24,314
Do or do not, there is no try.

7
00:00:26,567 --> 00:00:29,361
Heh. Did you just quote Star Wars?

8
00:00:30,821 --> 00:00:34,157
I believe I quoted Empire Strikes Back.

9
00:00:35,868 --> 00:00:38,453
Ha, ha. Oh, my God.

10
00:00:38,621 --> 00:00:42,166
I am lying in bed with a beautiful woman
who can quote Yoda.

11
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:43,834
[PENNY LAUGHS]

12
00:00:46,128 --> 00:00:47,254
[CHUCKLES]

13
00:00:48,297 --> 00:00:50,424
I love you, Penny.

14
00:00:55,054 --> 00:00:58,098
Uh.... Heh.

15
00:00:59,517 --> 00:01:01,685
Thank you.

16
00:01:04,397 --> 00:01:05,564
You're welcome.

17
00:01:07,608 --> 00:01:10,319
-I just wanted to put that out there.
-Oh, yeah. No, I--

18
00:01:10,486 --> 00:01:12,279
-I'm glad.
-Yeah-- Oh, good.

19
00:01:12,488 --> 00:01:13,739
-Good. Glad is good.
-Yeah.

20
00:01:14,115 --> 00:01:16,033
Ha. Ahem.

21
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:18,660
No-- Um.. ..

22
00:01:20,121 --> 00:01:22,123
So, heh....

23
00:01:22,582 --> 00:01:24,959
It's getting pretty late.
We should, tsk, go to sleep.

24
00:01:25,126 --> 00:01:26,210
-Yeah.
-Okay.

25
00:01:26,377 --> 00:01:27,586
Yeah, probably.

26
00:01:27,753 --> 00:01:30,213
-Okay. Good night, sweetie.
-Good night.

27
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:02,329
[TV PLAYING]

28
00:02:03,831 --> 00:02:08,043
Hey, Leonard,
where do you come down on giant ants?

29
00:02:09,337 --> 00:02:12,340
Sheldon says impossible,
Howard and I say not only possible...

30
00:02:12,506 --> 00:02:15,967
...but as a mode of transportation,
way cooler than the Batmobile.

31
00:02:16,844 --> 00:02:18,887
You are ignoring the square-cube law.

32
00:02:19,055 --> 00:02:22,391
The giant ant would be crushed
under the weight of its exoskeleton.

33
00:02:22,558 --> 00:02:26,061
For the record, the appropriate ranking
of cool modes of transportation...

34
00:02:26,228 --> 00:02:30,728
...is jetpack, hover board, transporter,
Batmobile and then giant ant.

35
00:02:32,485 --> 00:02:35,279
Seriously, you have nothing better
to do than sit around...

36
00:02:35,488 --> 00:02:38,908
...and discuss the possibility
of giant ants?

37
00:02:39,742 --> 00:02:42,369
-What's with him?
-Perhaps he's at a sensitive point...

38
00:02:42,536 --> 00:02:44,079
...In his monthly cycle.

39
00:02:46,374 --> 00:02:50,086
Are you saying he's man-struating?

40
00:02:51,087 --> 00:02:53,214
Not literally.

41
00:02:53,381 --> 00:02:55,424
But as far back as the 17th century...

42
00:02:55,591 --> 00:02:59,011
...scientists observed a 33-day
fluctuation in men's hormone levels.

43
00:02:59,428 --> 00:03:00,762
Interesting.

44
00:03:00,930 --> 00:03:04,350
That might explain my weepy days
in the middle of the month.

45
00:03:06,602 --> 00:03:08,103
You know what I'm talking about.

46
00:03:13,150 --> 00:03:15,360
Okay, forget giant ants.

47
00:03:15,569 --> 00:03:17,529
How about giant rabbits?

48
00:03:18,823 --> 00:03:20,616
Big or small, I don't like rabbits.

49
00:03:20,783 --> 00:03:24,453
They always look like they're about
to say something, but they never do.

50
00:03:24,912 --> 00:03:28,123
Rabbits do have a respiratory system
that would support great size.

51
00:03:28,290 --> 00:03:30,792
On a side note,
they are one of the few mammals...

52
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:33,879
...whose scrotum
is in front of the penis.

53
00:03:36,632 --> 00:03:39,051
Maybe that's
what they wanna talk about.

54
00:03:39,969 --> 00:03:43,806
Leonard, where do you stand
on giant rabbits and scrotal position?

55
00:03:44,974 --> 00:03:46,600
I honestly don't care.

56
00:03:46,767 --> 00:03:49,853
Really? Every time we've talked
about unusual animal genitals...

57
00:03:50,062 --> 00:03:53,315
...you've always had some pretty strong
and controversial opinions.

58
00:03:55,317 --> 00:03:57,694
What do you want?
I just don't give a rat’s ass.

59
00:03:57,903 --> 00:04:00,655
Would that be a giant rat's ass?

60
00:04:01,490 --> 00:04:04,367
For the record, giant rats are possible.

61
00:04:04,577 --> 00:04:06,495
Can we please talk
about something else?

62
00:04:06,662 --> 00:04:09,998
Maybe something vaguely related
to life as we know it on this planet?

63
00:04:10,332 --> 00:04:14,832
Okay, how about this for a topic:
"Why is Leonard being a giant douche?"

64
00:04:17,131 --> 00:04:19,967
Assuming giant douches are possible.

65
00:04:20,384 --> 00:04:23,345
Of course they are.
Leonard's being one.

66
00:04:24,722 --> 00:04:28,142
-Maybe he's having a spat with Penny.
-No. There was no spat.

67
00:04:28,350 --> 00:04:31,811
-Oh, but something happened.
- I don't wanna talk about it.

68
00:04:32,021 --> 00:04:36,025
But I sense you're going to and
I don't wanna hear about it. Excuse me.

69
00:04:36,817 --> 00:04:37,984
What'd you do, Romeo?

70
00:04:38,152 --> 00:04:40,320
Did you pour maple syrup
all over your body...

71
00:04:40,488 --> 00:04:43,449
...and ask her if she was in the mood
for a short stack?

72
00:04:47,870 --> 00:04:50,998
Think it would be funny
to put on her panties and jump around...

73
00:04:51,165 --> 00:04:53,458
...but it wound up
just creeping her out?

74
00:04:54,668 --> 00:04:58,421
-What”? No.
-Just asking, dude.

75
00:04:58,631 --> 00:05:00,215
It happens.

76
00:05:02,384 --> 00:05:04,302
You guys still on for bowling tonight?

77
00:05:04,512 --> 00:05:08,724
Oh, yes. In fact, I've prepared
some trash talk for the occasion. Ahem.

78
00:05:08,891 --> 00:05:11,143
You bowl like your mama.

79
00:05:12,394 --> 00:05:15,605
Unless she bowls well.
In which case, you bowl nothing like her.

80
00:05:16,732 --> 00:05:18,984
Oh. Ouch.

81
00:05:19,902 --> 00:05:23,572
That is what is referred to
as "a burn on you."”

82
00:05:24,865 --> 00:05:27,868
-Did you ask her to start waxing?
-No.

83
00:05:28,077 --> 00:05:30,996
-Did you start waxing?
-No.

84
00:05:31,705 --> 00:05:34,582
While making love,
did you accidentally spank your own ass...

85
00:05:34,750 --> 00:05:36,710
...and cry out, "Mommy"?

86
00:05:44,093 --> 00:05:45,886
I'm walking away from you now.

87
00:05:47,429 --> 00:05:50,932
-That wasn't a no.
-Yeah. Think we're getting close.

88
00:05:52,935 --> 00:05:55,812
Did you take a Benadryl
and fall asleep while pleasuring her?

89
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:58,399
Because you can die that way.

90
00:05:59,733 --> 00:06:01,443
Oh, that would be a good way to go.

91
00:06:03,946 --> 00:06:06,073
-Hi.
-Oh, hey.

92
00:06:06,282 --> 00:06:09,034
Good, Penny.
Reminder, bowling tonight at 7:00.

93
00:06:09,243 --> 00:06:11,119
Oh, right. Bowling.

94
00:06:11,328 --> 00:06:13,288
You don't have to come
if you don't want.

95
00:06:13,497 --> 00:06:17,375
No, no, it's okay. I mean, let's face it,
you would get creamed without me.

96
00:06:17,585 --> 00:06:19,795
We would indeed.
In this particular case...

97
00:06:19,962 --> 00:06:22,881
...your lack of femininity
works to our advantage.

98
00:06:24,508 --> 00:06:27,719
Yeah. It's always nice chatting with you,
Sheldon.

99
00:06:28,804 --> 00:06:32,516
-Sarcasm??
PENNY:: Thinly veiled contempt.

100
00:06:33,350 --> 00:06:35,643
-Remember, 7:00.
PENNY: Got it.

101
00:06:35,811 --> 00:06:38,230
-Pacific Daylight Time.
PENNY: Bite me.

102
00:06:39,481 --> 00:06:41,816
Please reserve that butch spirit
for the lanes.

103
00:06:49,491 --> 00:06:52,160
I thought you were bringing
your own bowling shoes.

104
00:06:52,328 --> 00:06:54,997
These are my own bowling shoes.

105
00:06:55,414 --> 00:06:57,124
Then what's with the disinfectant?

106
00:06:57,333 --> 00:06:59,668
I know where my feet have been.

107
00:07:04,131 --> 00:07:05,507
Hey, Penny.

108
00:07:05,841 --> 00:07:06,925
And you guys.

109
00:07:08,802 --> 00:07:11,679
Albino Bob couldn't make it,
so I brought a substitute.

110
00:07:11,847 --> 00:07:15,809
I believe some of you
know Wil Wheaton.

111
00:07:18,729 --> 00:07:20,272
Hi, Sheldon. How's it going?

112
00:07:20,481 --> 00:07:24,526
Well, well, well,
if it isn't Wil Wheaton.

113
00:07:24,693 --> 00:07:27,028
The Green Goblin to my Spider-Man.

114
00:07:27,196 --> 00:07:29,489
The Pope Paul V to my Galileo.

115
00:07:29,657 --> 00:07:32,785
The Internet Explorer to my Firefox.

116
00:07:33,410 --> 00:07:37,205
Not carrying a grudge because I beat you
at that card tournament, are you?

117
00:07:37,373 --> 00:07:40,084
I'm the proud owner
of Wil-Wheaton-stinks.com...

118
00:07:40,292 --> 00:07:42,544
...dot-net and dot-org.
What does that tell you?

119
00:07:42,753 --> 00:07:46,173
It tells me that I am living rent-free
right here.

120
00:07:47,549 --> 00:07:50,051
-You ready to bowl?
-Oh, I'm ready.

121
00:07:50,219 --> 00:07:53,055
I don't know if Stuart told you
what you're up against...

122
00:07:53,222 --> 00:07:57,059
...but before you stands the co-captain
of the East Texas Christian Youth...

123
00:07:57,226 --> 00:07:59,978
...Holy Roller Bowling League
Championship team.

124
00:08:01,313 --> 00:08:03,523
Seven-to-12-year-old division.

125
00:08:03,899 --> 00:08:05,734
Also, Penny's pretty good.

126
00:08:06,777 --> 00:08:08,195
[CLICKS TONGUE]

127
00:08:08,696 --> 00:08:11,573
Great. Then it's on.

128
00:08:12,616 --> 00:08:14,951
Foolish Wil Wheaton.

129
00:08:15,119 --> 00:08:17,454
It was never off.

130
00:08:20,207 --> 00:08:21,458
Yes!

131
00:08:21,667 --> 00:08:23,418
A common spare.

132
00:08:23,585 --> 00:08:27,046
The Miss Congeniality
of the bowling pageant.

133
00:08:27,423 --> 00:08:30,551
Before you jump on Twitter
to tout your modest accomplishment...

134
00:08:30,759 --> 00:08:33,052
...watch how it's really done.

135
00:08:33,262 --> 00:08:35,639
I am the ball.

136
00:08:37,099 --> 00:08:39,226
My thoughts are its thoughts.

137
00:08:39,393 --> 00:08:41,770
Its holes are my holes.

138
00:08:50,821 --> 00:08:52,531
Yes.

139
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:53,866
Tweet that, Tweety Bird.

140
00:08:56,618 --> 00:08:59,412
-I just wanted to tell you I'm a big fan.
-Oh, thanks.

141
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:02,457
I'm sure you're probably sick
of Star Trek questions...

142
00:09:02,624 --> 00:09:04,834
...but Whoopi Goldberg,
you ever hit that?

143
00:09:10,007 --> 00:09:11,633
Ah. Beer.

144
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:16,300
The magic elixir that can turn this poor,
shy Indian boy into the life of the party.

145
00:09:22,144 --> 00:09:23,812
Oh, yeah.

146
00:09:26,148 --> 00:09:29,526
-Chili-cheese fry?
-Yes. I love chili-cheese fries.

147
00:09:29,735 --> 00:09:32,279
-Really? You love them?
-Yeah, why?

148
00:09:32,488 --> 00:09:34,031
No reason. Just glad to hear...

149
00:09:34,198 --> 00:09:36,825
...you're comfortable
saying you love something.

150
00:09:38,994 --> 00:09:41,788
-You wanna get into this right now?
-Get into what?

151
00:09:41,955 --> 00:09:44,123
Why wouldn't you love
the chili-cheese fries?

152
00:09:44,291 --> 00:09:46,209
They've been in your life a long time.

153
00:09:46,418 --> 00:09:49,379
They make you happy.
They deserve to know.

154
00:09:50,005 --> 00:09:53,967
Okay, look, you caught me by surprise
last night. I didn't know what to say.

155
00:09:54,176 --> 00:09:57,095
Now you've had time to think about it.
What do you wanna say?

156
00:09:57,554 --> 00:10:00,348
-I'm not sure.
-How can you not be sure?

157
00:10:00,557 --> 00:10:02,392
-This isn't the place to have this.
-No.

158
00:10:02,601 --> 00:10:05,687
The place was in bed after I said,
"I love you"...

159
00:10:05,854 --> 00:10:08,147
...and you said,
"Thank you. Good night."

160
00:10:08,857 --> 00:10:11,734
-Don't push it, Leonard.
-I am not pushing anything.

161
00:10:11,944 --> 00:10:16,073
You are. You don't get to decide
when I'm ready to say "I love you."

162
00:10:19,868 --> 00:10:23,830
Ah. The premature "I love you."

163
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:27,501
I guessed premature. Does that count?

164
00:10:33,841 --> 00:10:35,467
Penny.

165
00:10:35,926 --> 00:10:37,552
Penny.

166
00:10:38,679 --> 00:10:40,263
Penny.

167
00:10:41,849 --> 00:10:44,268
-What?
-This is for you.

168
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:49,272
-Ice cream?
-I've been familiarizing myself...

169
00:10:49,439 --> 00:10:53,939
...with female emotional crises
by studying the comic strip "Cathy."

170
00:10:56,488 --> 00:11:00,283
When she's upset,
she says "ack" and eats ice cream.

171
00:11:03,412 --> 00:11:05,205
Um....

172
00:11:05,372 --> 00:11:06,539
Ack.

173
00:11:08,584 --> 00:11:11,712
And if you were a cat,
I would have brought you a lasagne.

174
00:11:13,505 --> 00:11:15,381
Did Leonard send you over here?

175
00:11:15,591 --> 00:11:19,094
No. We haven't spoken
since your abrupt departure last night...

176
00:11:19,261 --> 00:11:22,806
...caused us to forfeit to Stuart
and his dastardly ringer, Wil Wheaton.

177
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:24,932
Yeah, I'm sorry about that.

178
00:11:25,142 --> 00:11:28,395
Not too proud to admit
that I cried myself to sleep.

179
00:11:29,271 --> 00:11:31,064
-Again, I'm sorry.
-Let me tell you...

180
00:11:31,231 --> 00:11:32,732
...Sleep did not come easily...

181
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:36,695
...with Leonard in the next room
singing along with Alanis Morissette.

182
00:11:38,697 --> 00:11:39,948
-You're kidding.
-No.

183
00:11:40,157 --> 00:11:42,534
Clearly another woman
in dire need of ice cream.

184
00:11:44,286 --> 00:11:46,913
What part of this is supposed
to make me feel better?

185
00:11:47,122 --> 00:11:50,291
The part where I tell you
I've engineered a rematch...

186
00:11:50,459 --> 00:11:52,169
...with Stuart's team for tonight.

187
00:11:52,377 --> 00:11:56,089
Oh, honey, I don't know. Things
are a little weird with Leonard right now.

188
00:11:56,590 --> 00:12:00,010
You want me to remove him from the team?
I'm the captain, I can do that.

189
00:12:01,470 --> 00:12:05,265
No, no, that's okay. Just let me
talk to him and I'll get back to you.

190
00:12:06,391 --> 00:12:10,311
-When are you going to talk to him?
- I don't know.

191
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:13,564
He's in the laundry room now.
Now would be a good time.

192
00:12:13,815 --> 00:12:15,775
You're not gonna leave me
until I do it?

193
00:12:15,984 --> 00:12:18,945
Oh, I think we both know
the answer to that question.

194
00:12:25,369 --> 00:12:29,247
- I think we should talk now.
-What? No, it's okay.

195
00:12:29,414 --> 00:12:32,291
We don't have to talk because
there's nothing to talk about.

196
00:12:32,459 --> 00:12:34,836
-Everything's good.
-Really?

197
00:12:35,003 --> 00:12:36,337
So you didn't get snarky...

198
00:12:36,505 --> 00:12:39,549
...because I said something nice
to a bowl of chili fries?

199
00:12:40,842 --> 00:12:43,135
All right, maybe I overreacted.

200
00:12:43,303 --> 00:12:46,139
So we're in two different places,
emotionally. So what?

201
00:12:46,473 --> 00:12:49,184
And maybe I'm a little ahead of you,
and that's fine.

202
00:12:49,393 --> 00:12:51,728
In fact, it makes sense,
because let's face it. ..

203
00:12:51,895 --> 00:12:54,731
...I've been In this relationship
two years longer than you.

204
00:12:57,234 --> 00:13:00,320
Look, Leonard, you have to know
how much I care about you.

205
00:13:00,487 --> 00:13:03,406
It's just that I've said the I word
too soon before. ..

206
00:13:03,573 --> 00:13:05,283
...and it didn't work out very well.

207
00:13:05,701 --> 00:13:08,495
Really?
I wouldn't know what that's like.

208
00:13:09,204 --> 00:13:10,413
I'm sorry.

209
00:13:10,580 --> 00:13:12,790
-You know what I'm talking about.
-Yeah, I do.

210
00:13:14,251 --> 00:13:17,212
-So we're good?
-Yes, that's what I'm telling you.

211
00:13:17,379 --> 00:13:19,089
We are good. We are great.

212
00:13:19,256 --> 00:13:22,550
All right. Fence mended,
problem swept under the rug.

213
00:13:22,718 --> 00:13:24,136
Time to bowl.

214
00:13:26,054 --> 00:13:28,347
Yes, I was eavesdropping.
There's a lot at stake.

215
00:13:31,601 --> 00:13:33,311
Attention, all bowlers...

216
00:13:33,478 --> 00:13:37,978
...I've taken the liberty
of having these made for our rematch.

217
00:13:39,109 --> 00:13:41,694
-The Wesley Crushers?
-No, not the Wesley Crushers.

218
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:44,030
The Wesley "Crushers.”

219
00:13:44,448 --> 00:13:46,533
- don't get it.
-Wesley Crusher...

220
00:13:46,742 --> 00:13:48,994
...was Wil Wheaton's character
on Star Trek.

221
00:13:49,161 --> 00:13:50,620
Still don't get it.

222
00:13:50,829 --> 00:13:52,872
It's a blindingly clever play on words.

223
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:55,959
By appropriating his character's
name and adding the S...

224
00:13:56,126 --> 00:14:00,088
...we imply that we will be
the crushers of Wesley.

225
00:14:01,506 --> 00:14:03,466
I'm sorry, but the Wesley Crushers...

226
00:14:03,633 --> 00:14:05,926
...sounds like people
who like Wesley Crusher.

227
00:14:06,136 --> 00:14:08,179
No, again,
it's not the Wesley Crushers.

228
00:14:08,347 --> 00:14:10,515
It's the Wesley "Crushers.”

229
00:14:12,434 --> 00:14:15,395
No, if you want it to mean
you're crushing Wesley...

230
00:14:15,562 --> 00:14:17,522
...it'd be the "Wesley" Crushers.

231
00:14:17,731 --> 00:14:20,817
Do you people even hear yourselves?
It's not the Wesley Crushers.

232
00:14:20,984 --> 00:14:25,029
It's not the "Wesley" Crushers,
it's Wesley "Crushers."

233
00:14:25,197 --> 00:14:27,741
Hey, look.
They named their team after me.

234
00:14:29,159 --> 00:14:31,953
No, it's not-- Never mind.

235
00:14:34,414 --> 00:14:37,750
So we're all clear on the bet
and the stakes?

236
00:14:37,918 --> 00:14:39,002
Oh, yes.

237
00:14:39,169 --> 00:14:43,339
The losers will be publicly humiliated
in a fashion to be chosen by the victor.

238
00:14:43,548 --> 00:14:47,260
FYI, I plan on having you
publish a scientific paper...

239
00:14:47,427 --> 00:14:50,638
...expounding the discredited
Belakovsky hypotheses.

240
00:14:52,474 --> 00:14:53,975
Ouch again.

241
00:14:56,186 --> 00:14:57,937
Hey, Sheldon.

242
00:14:58,313 --> 00:15:01,607
I wanted you to know I'm looking forward
to wiping the floor with you.

243
00:15:01,817 --> 00:15:05,821
Oh, yes”? Well, before I respond,
let me ask you a question.

244
00:15:06,822 --> 00:15:09,950
Is your mother a good or poor bowler?

245
00:15:16,373 --> 00:15:19,084
-After you.
-No, after you.

246
00:15:19,251 --> 00:15:23,672
As we are currently crushing you,
Wesley.

247
00:15:25,799 --> 00:15:29,135
It's customary for the player
on the right-hand lane to bowl first.

248
00:15:31,304 --> 00:15:32,847
All right.

249
00:15:41,022 --> 00:15:42,565
It's a custom, not a rule.

250
00:15:43,817 --> 00:15:45,944
I so loathe you.

251
00:15:46,987 --> 00:15:50,156
That's right, Sheldon.
Embrace the dark side.

252
00:15:52,784 --> 00:15:55,995
That's not even from your franchise.

253
00:15:57,205 --> 00:16:01,705
I, um-- I want you to know that
even though we're on opposite sides...

254
00:16:02,002 --> 00:16:03,837
...I bear you no ill will.

255
00:16:05,046 --> 00:16:07,673
-Thank you, Stuart. It's nice to know.
-Mm-hm.

256
00:16:07,883 --> 00:16:10,844
People from opposite sides
often have good relationships.

257
00:16:11,052 --> 00:16:12,595
You know, Romeo and Juliet...

258
00:16:12,804 --> 00:16:16,140
...Tony and Maria from West Side Story.

259
00:16:16,725 --> 00:16:19,894
What's-his-name
and the big, blue chick in Avatar.

260
00:16:22,397 --> 00:16:24,399
I'm gonna bowl| now.

261
00:16:26,818 --> 00:16:28,277
Be the ball, Howard.

262
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:30,696
Leave me alone, Sheldon.

263
00:16:39,372 --> 00:16:40,748
You weren't the ball.

264
00:16:43,877 --> 00:16:45,461
Hey, thanks.

265
00:16:45,629 --> 00:16:47,380
-This is fun, huh?
-Yeah.

266
00:16:47,547 --> 00:16:49,382
It's good we got out
and did something physical.

267
00:16:49,591 --> 00:16:52,051
-Mm-hm.
-Gets us out of our heads.

268
00:16:52,219 --> 00:16:53,261
You get in your head...

269
00:16:53,428 --> 00:16:56,431
...you start to over-think, over-analyze,
obsess, you worry.

270
00:16:56,598 --> 00:17:00,018
That's not what we're doing tonight.
We're throwing a ball at some pins.

271
00:17:00,227 --> 00:17:01,436
-Yeah, that's right.
-Mm-hm.

272
00:17:01,645 --> 00:17:04,689
And someday, we don't know when,
maybe you'll love me back.

273
00:17:07,609 --> 00:17:09,402
Ooh. I'm up.

274
00:17:11,321 --> 00:17:14,657
ALL [CHANTING]:
Sheldon. Sheldon. Sheldon.

275
00:17:14,824 --> 00:17:15,950
Excuse me.

276
00:17:16,159 --> 00:17:20,079
I don't know who you're chanting for,
as I am currently the ball.

277
00:17:22,332 --> 00:17:26,832
ALL [CHANTING]:
The ball. The ball. The ball.

278
00:17:31,216 --> 00:17:32,258
Thank you, Jesus!

279
00:17:35,136 --> 00:17:36,387
As my mother would say.

280
00:17:42,018 --> 00:17:44,645
I'm glad you patched things up
with your boyfriend.

281
00:17:44,813 --> 00:17:46,689
Yeah, me too.

282
00:17:46,856 --> 00:17:49,900
It's tough when the I bomb
gets dropped and you're not ready.

283
00:17:50,068 --> 00:17:51,402
Tell me about it.

284
00:17:52,988 --> 00:17:56,074
I dated this one girl,
and I told her that I loved her...

285
00:17:56,533 --> 00:17:58,451
and she said she wasn't sure.

286
00:17:59,077 --> 00:18:02,580
And she strung me along
for almost two years. It was brutal.

287
00:18:03,123 --> 00:18:05,834
-Oh, I'm sorry.
-Thanks.

288
00:18:06,376 --> 00:18:08,753
I wish she had just broken up with me
right there.

289
00:18:09,421 --> 00:18:11,256
Put me out of my misery.

290
00:18:11,423 --> 00:18:13,550
-Really?
Yeah. Would have been kinder.

291
00:18:14,009 --> 00:18:16,302
-Wil, you're up.
-Oh, that's me.

292
00:18:21,766 --> 00:18:23,726
Did you let Wil Wheaton
get in your head?

293
00:18:23,935 --> 00:18:26,103
-What are you talking about?
-He's evil.

294
00:18:26,271 --> 00:18:28,231
He plays evil mind games.

295
00:18:28,398 --> 00:18:30,733
-Did he tell you his grandmother died?
-No.

296
00:18:30,942 --> 00:18:34,987
If he does, don't believe it. He's not above
playing the dead meemaw card.

297
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:39,784
Yes!

298
00:18:40,952 --> 00:18:43,120
Enjoy the accolades now,
Wil Wheaton.

299
00:18:43,288 --> 00:18:45,748
But like your time on
Star Trek: Next Generation...

300
00:18:45,915 --> 00:18:48,500
...your smug self-satisfaction
will be short-lived.

301
00:18:50,378 --> 00:18:52,546
-Penny, you're up.
-All right, remember...

302
00:18:52,714 --> 00:18:56,300
-...his meemaw's alive and be the ball.
-Yeah. I got it.

303
00:18:56,468 --> 00:18:59,012
-Oh, we really need a strike here.
- I know.

304
00:18:59,220 --> 00:19:02,264
-Take your time and concentrate.
-Leonard, stop pressuring me.

305
00:19:02,432 --> 00:19:04,725
-I'm not pressuring you.
-You are. Just back off.

306
00:19:05,685 --> 00:19:07,520
Okay. I'm sorry. I'll shut up.

307
00:19:09,689 --> 00:19:11,273
I didn't mean shut up.

308
00:19:11,608 --> 00:19:12,775
Fine.

309
00:19:12,942 --> 00:19:15,235
Just tell me what to do and I'll do it.

310
00:19:16,488 --> 00:19:17,530
[SIGHS]

311
00:19:17,697 --> 00:19:20,741
No. This isn't fair to you, Leonard.
I'm sorry.

312
00:19:22,452 --> 00:19:24,871
Wait, where are you going?
Penny, come back.

313
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:26,247
I'll get you ice cream.

314
00:19:26,956 --> 00:19:29,959
-No, let her go.
-Are you insane?

315
00:19:30,126 --> 00:19:31,961
If she leaves, it's over.

316
00:19:32,545 --> 00:19:35,214
Pretty sure it's already over.

317
00:19:36,257 --> 00:19:37,841
WIL:
Tough luck, Sheldon.

318
00:19:39,719 --> 00:19:41,887
You did this, didn't you?

319
00:19:42,097 --> 00:19:45,391
Do you think I would break up a couple
just to win a bowling match?

320
00:19:46,476 --> 00:19:49,729
-No, I suppose not.
-Good. Keep thinking that.

321
00:19:53,650 --> 00:19:56,944
Wheaton....

322
00:20:00,323 --> 00:20:01,991
Mm-hm. Mm-hm. Yep.

323
00:20:02,158 --> 00:20:06,620
I'm telling you, the Match.com chicks
are much looser than on eHarmony.

324
00:20:08,623 --> 00:20:13,123
Oh. You know, I gotta call you back.
I won a bet and it's time to collect.

325
00:20:27,976 --> 00:20:31,813
I don't know about you,
but I feel empowered.

326
00:20:59,674 --> 00:21:01,676
[ENGLISH - US - SDH]

